# Who gets asked to review what.
#
# One maintainer today, so most of this is routing rather than gatekeeping:
# GitHub requests a review from the owner of every path a pull request touches.
# The paths listed separately are the ones where a change is easy to make and
# expensive to get wrong, and they are the commitments AGENTS.md and
# CONTRIBUTING.md say must not erode. Listing them is also a note to a future
# second maintainer about which files deserve a slower read.

*                                   @lhadhazy

# The articles' code, published in part 1 § 3 and compared field for field
# against the markdown by tests/test_post_conformance.py. qedro also generates
# its published Art. 30 facet schema from Processing here, so a change is a
# change to somebody else's published schema too.
/src/pipeline_runtime/descriptor.py @lhadhazy
/src/pipeline_runtime/errors.py     @lhadhazy

# Byte-identical to the descriptors the articles quote, comments included.
/example/                           @lhadhazy

# The OpenLineage facet schemas the articles describe and
# docs/post-corrections.md discusses.
/schemas/                           @lhadhazy

# Releases. Pushing a `v*` tag publishes to PyPI, where a version number can
# never be reused.
/.github/workflows/                 @lhadhazy
/pyproject.toml                     @lhadhazy
/CHANGELOG.md                       @lhadhazy

